    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nYes, indeed there is an extra `InsertLeave` event.\r\n\r\nThis is fixable by tweaking `'eventignore'` option to temporarily have `InsertLeave` event. However, as `<CR>` (and any other 'mini.pairs' mapping) is used quite frequently, the goal is to have them the least amount of overhead as possible. So not quite sure what is the best approach here.\r\n\r\nMaybe, the most straightforward here is for Neovim to not update diagnostic if it comes after `<C-o>` (that is, not regular Normal mode, but slightly different).\r\n\r\nMeanwhile, you can use the following remap:\r\n```lua\r\n_G.cr_noinsertleave = function()\r\n  local cache_eventignore = vim.o.eventignore\r\n  vim.o.eventignore = 'InsertLeave'\r\n  vim.schedule(function() vim.o.eventignore = cache_eventignore end)\r\n  return MiniPairs.cr()\r\nend\r\nvim.keymap.set('i', '<CR>', 'v:lua.cr_noinsertleave()', { expr = true })\r\n```",
            "created_at": "2023-12-23T09:50:37Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/626#issuecomment-1868256077",
